   "title": "Pernod Ricard India sales grow 19% in Sept qtr; IPO plan awaits board approval",
   "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"
  }
 ],
 "synopsis": "French spirits maker Pernod Ricard reported a 19 percent sales growth in India for the September quarter, driven by strong market demand, ongoing premiumisation trends, and preparatory measures for a potential initial public offering. The company brought forward some shipments to ensure uninterrupted supplies during a transition involving a name change and product relabelling, creating a favourable pipe-fill effect that benefited Q1 sales. While the board has instructed management to continue taking preparatory steps for a potential IPO, the final decision to proceed remains subject to board approval.",
